&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;m_-113912706363268805m_-2746164444908759431gmail-docs-internal-guid-131e4fb0-7fff-b4e9-ff50-e8cf32449b1b&quot;&gt;CoreWeave is The Essential Cloud for AI™. Built for pioneers by pioneers, CoreWeave delivers a platform of technology, tools, and teams that enables innovators to build and scale AI with confidence. Trusted by leading AI labs, startups, and global enterprises, CoreWeave combines superior infrastructure performance with deep technical expertise to accelerate breakthroughs and turn compute into capability. Founded in 2017, CoreWeave became a publicly traded company (Nasdaq: CRWV) in March 2025. Learn more at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coreweave.com&quot;&gt;www.coreweave.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;We&#39;re proud to be a Living Wage accredited Employer.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Director, Enterprise Business Development – EMEA will report to the Vice President and Managing Director, EMEA and lead the strategy and execution model for CoreWeave’s Enterprise business across the region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a business development and strategy leadership role that works through CoreWeave’s field organisation. Country sales teams will retain account ownership, opportunity management and revenue responsibility, while you define the Enterprise strategy, customer propositions, industry points of view, sales plays and adoption mechanisms that enable them to win and grow strategic Enterprise customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with Field Sales, Product, Field Engineering, Product and Field Marketing, partners and customers to build a differentiated Enterprise narrative and translate it into repeatable field execution. You will also build and lead a team of Enterprise Business Development Managers aligned to priority vertical industries, bringing deep expertise in how AI will reshape those sectors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In This Role, You Will&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and execute CoreWeave’s EMEA Enterprise business development strategy in partnership with regional and country sales leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish CoreWeave’s Enterprise point of view, including Enterprise architecture, market segmentation, AI wallet distribution, buying centres, workload evolution and competitive positioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define how CoreWeave participates in the Enterprise AI transformation journey, from initial AI initiatives through production adoption, operationalisation and scaled Enterprise Intelligence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop the narrative for how CoreWeave enables customers to operate their AI Learning Loops, positioning the platform as the infrastructure, software and operational foundation through which organisations continuously build, deploy, learn and improve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a systematic view of Enterprise AI adoption across EMEA, including where investment is occurring, which workloads are moving into production, how budgets are shifting and where CoreWeave can gain market share.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define Enterprise segmentation and prioritisation models that help field teams identify the customers, industries, workloads and buying centres with the greatest strategic and commercial potential.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop CoreWeave’s Enterprise sales plays, including target customer profiles, business triggers, technical use cases, executive value propositions, competitive positioning and expansion motions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the development of Enterprise sales content, executive narratives, pitch decks and field assets in partnership with Field and Product Marketing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a repeatable Enterprise adoption methodology that helps customers progress from initial workload evaluation through production deployment, scaled consumption and broader platform adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop programmes that enable customers to adopt CoreWeave as a strategic component of their AI architecture rather than as a point solution for individual workloads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product leadership to ensure CoreWeave’s Enterprise strategy reflects product capabilities, roadmap direction and the requirements of large-scale Enterprise customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate customer and market insight into clear recommendations for product investment, developer experience, security, governance, observability, integration and Enterprise platform capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Field Engineering to define Enterprise adoption strategies using Forward Deployed Engineers, specialist technical resources and services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build repeatable engagement models that combine business, technical and operational resources around the most important Enterprise transformation opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Field Sales leaders to translate Enterprise strategy into country and account-level execution, ensuring sellers understand where to focus, what to lead with and how to progress customers through the adoption journey.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with partners to build joint Enterprise propositions, solution patterns and routes to market that accelerate customer adoption and extend CoreWeave’s reach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain executive-level relationships with strategic Enterprise customers, technology partners and ecosystem leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as an executive sponsor for strategically important Enterprise transformation opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain an active graph of Enterprise AI adoption across the region, mapping customers, industries, workloads, AI investment, architecture choices, partners, competitors and stages of maturity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, lead and develop a team of Enterprise Business Development Managers aligned to priority industry segments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure each industry leader develops a differentiated view of how AI will reshape their sector, including priority use cases, economic impact, data and infrastructure requirements, buying centres, barriers to adoption and relevant ecosystem partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish a rigorous operating cadence and scorecard covering market penetration, Enterprise adoption, field execution, pipeline influence, consumption, revenue performance and market share.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent CoreWeave’s Enterprise narrative externally with customers, partners, industry bodies, analysts, media and at major industry events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Objectives&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;During the first 12 months, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define CoreWeave’s EMEA Enterprise strategy, operating plan and growth priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish a clear Enterprise segmentation model covering priority industries, customers, workloads and buying centres.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop CoreWeave’s Enterprise architecture and AI transformation points of view.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the Enterprise AI Learning Loop narrative and articulate how CoreWeave becomes the ways and means through which customers operate and scale those loops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the initial Enterprise sales plays, executive narratives, sales content and pitch materials required by field teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and launch a repeatable Enterprise adoption methodology covering evaluation, production deployment, expansion and scaled adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the engagement model for Forward Deployed Engineers, Field Engineering and services within strategic Enterprise opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain the first regional Enterprise AI adoption graph, identifying market penetration, wallet distribution, major workloads, competitive positions and whitespace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish the vertical industry strategy and determine the first priority industry segments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire and onboard the initial Enterprise Business Development Managers aligned to those industries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build executive relationships with an initial set of strategic Enterprise customers and partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish the business review cadence, measurement framework and market-share methodology for the Enterprise segment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate measurable contribution to Enterprise pipeline, adoption, consumption and overall EMEA Enterprise revenue performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of experience in enterprise business development, go-to-market strategy, sales, industry leadership, consulting or product strategy within cloud infrastructure, enterprise technology, AI or another complex technology environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience defining and executing Enterprise growth strategies across multiple markets or industries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven record of translating market and customer insight into repeatable sales plays, adoption programmes and measurable commercial outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of how large Enterprises evaluate, adopt, govern and scale new technology platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of Enterprise architecture, cloud infrastructure, AI platforms, data environments and the operational requirements of production AI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing segmentation models, executive value propositions, sales plays, industry narratives and adoption methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to connect technical architecture with business strategy, operating-model change and executive priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working closely with field sales organisations to improve customer targeting, opportunity development, competitive positioning and expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with Product and Engineering teams to translate Enterprise requirements into roadmap and investment priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing or leading complex customer adoption programmes involving specialist engineering, consulting, services or Forward Deployed teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of the Enterprise AI buying landscape, including technology budgets, buying centres, strategic partners and evolving workload economics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience building senior relationships with CIOs, CTOs, CDOs, business leaders and other Enterprise executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing industry-specific strategies or leading business development across major Enterprise verticals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical capability, with the ability to build market models, adoption frameworks, segmentation strategies and executive-level business reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building, hiring, coaching and developing high-performing business development, strategy or industry teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead through influence across Sales, Product, Engineering, Marketing and partner organisations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A record of operating successfully across EMEA markets and cultures, with the ability to travel regularly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leadership experience in Enterprise strategy, business development, industry go-to-market or sales at a major hyperscale cloud provider, AI platform company or global infrastructure technology business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience building or scaling an Enterprise cloud or AI business measured through customer adoption, consumption, revenue and market share.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience defining Enterprise architecture or transformation points of view used by large customer-facing organisations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building AI, cloud or data-platform adoption methodologies for large Enterprise customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Forward Deployed Engineering, professional services, transformation consulting or other high-touch Enterprise adoption models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in one or more major Enterprise industries and a strong understanding of how AI will change industry value chains, operating models and economics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing public-facing thought leadership and representing a technology company with customers, analysts, media and at major industry events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established executive relationships across the EMEA Enterprise and technology ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bachelor’s degree or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wondering If You’re a Good Fit?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in investing in our people and value candidates who bring different experiences, even if they do not meet every requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a builder. You are comfortable starting with an ambition, creating the model and then driving it into execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can turn a complex technology and market landscape into a clear point of view that customers and field teams can act on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can move comfortably between a CIO, a product leader, a field seller, an engineer and an industry executive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You influence through clarity, credibility and conviction rather than positional authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You understand that great strategy only matters if the field can execute it consistently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a confident spokesperson who can represent CoreWeave’s Enterprise narrative in executive meetings, on stage and with the media.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are motivated by building a category and changing how Enterprises think about AI infrastructure, not simply competing for individual transactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why CoreWeave?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At CoreWeave, we work hard, have fun and move fast. We’re in an exciting stage of hyper-growth, we’re not afraid of a little chaos and we’re constantly learning.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team cares deeply about how we build our product and how we work together, which is represented through our core values:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be Curious at Your Core&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act Like an Owner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empower Employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver Best-in-Class Client Experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Achieve More Together&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We support an entrepreneurial outlook and independent thinking, and foster an environment that encourages collaboration and innovative solutions to complex problems. You will be surrounded by some of the best talent in the industry, with the opportunity to help shape CoreWeave’s future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The starting salary will be determined by job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and the market location. We strive for both market alignment and internal equity when determining compensation. In addition to base salary, our total rewards package includes a discretionary bonus, equity awards, and a comprehensive benefits program (all based on eligibility).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;To fulfill our obligation to protect client data, successful applicants offered employment with CoreWeave will be required to complete a basic criminal record check, conducted in compliance with GDPR. Employment offers are conditional upon receiving satisfactory check results.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to a competitive salary, we offer a variety of benefits to support your needs, including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family-level Medical Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family-level Dental Insurance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous Pension Contribution&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life Assurance at 4x Salary&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Critical Illness Cover&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Assistance Programme&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tuition Reimbursement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work culture focused on innovative disruption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Benefits may vary by location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;CoreWeave is an equal opportunity employer, committed to fostering an inclusive and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants and candidates will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recruitment Agencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;CoreWeave does not accept speculative CVs. Any unsolicited CVs received will be treated as the property of CoreWeave and your Terms &amp;amp; Conditions associated with the use of CVs will be considered null and void.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Any unsolicited CVs sent by your company to us – that is to say, in any situation where we have not directly engaged your company in writing to supply candidates for a specific vacancy – will be considered by us to be a “free gift”, leaving us liable for no fees whatsoever should we choose to contact the candidate directly and engage the candidate’s services, and will in no way establish any prior claim by your company to representation of that candidate should the candidate’s details also be submitted by any other party.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Export Control Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This position requires access to technology and/or source code subject to U.S. export control laws. Any such access will be provided only in compliance with applicable U.S. export control requirements. As part of the recruitment process, CoreWeave may request limited information reasonably necessary to assess applicable export-control requirements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
