&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Are curious about people and love to speak, build and nurture relations;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Are an excellent communicator (especially) verbally and in writing;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Are well-organised and display the ability to structure and prioritise their work.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Startdate&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Flexible&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The role is onsite, Monday to Friday, based in our offices at Buckingham Gate. It is essential we work at a fast pace and collaborate in person to create market-leading, unmatched events throughout the calendar year. It will be great to have you as part of our team.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Help make the world more hospitable &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The hospitality industry is uniquely human, and it deserves technology that’s just as inspiring as the people behind it. At Mews, we’re transforming the industry with a platform that helps hotels run smarter, move faster and create better guest experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work with smart, curious people who care deeply about what they do. You’ll have autonomy and the trust to make good decisions and move quickly. And you’ll enjoy a real sense of purpose as you see the impact of what we’re building.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re motivated by ownership, curiosity and meaningful impact, and are driven to deliver consistent high performance, you’ll feel at home here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Let&#39;s get into the specifics. It’s impossible to capture every nuance of a role – especially at a rapidly growing company like Mews – but if we had to distil it into a job description (which we do because this is a job description), it would be this:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;You would own Mews&#39; relationships with the press, turning company news, product launches and leadership insight into credible coverage across hospitality, travel, technology and business media. This is a new role, the first dedicated media relations seat at Mews, so the contacts you build and the way you work will set the standard for how we deal with the press. Hospitality technology offers good stories and unusual data to pitch, and leaders here respond to press requests within about a day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You would join the Communications team within Marketing and work closely with the communications lead, the colleagues who shape our stories, and leadership, product marketing and regional marketing. Day to day you would pitch journalists directly, host press briefings, handle inbound enquiries and prepare leaders to speak well in front of the press. The role is remote first in Europe, ideally near London, Berlin or Paris where many of the journalists we work with are based, with about 10% travel to meet press and attend events such as Unfold.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Journalists respond to people they know and trust, not to mass pitches, and the strongest coverage comes from a specialist who holds those relationships personally. Mews has strong stories and data to offer, and this role exists so that someone owns that conversation: choosing the right journalist for each story, answering inbound questions quickly and accurately, and knowing when to escalate something sensitive. Done well, it builds the company&#39;s reputation with the people who cover our industry over the long term.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you would do&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain direct relationships with journalists across hospitality, travel, technology and business media: develop stories with the communications team, pitch them proactively by phone and email, host press briefings and invite journalists to events such as Unfold.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond to inbound press enquiries (currently two to three a week and growing) quickly and accurately, and escalate anything potentially sensitive to the communications lead straight away.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Brief and coach executive and local spokespeople, and share what you learn from journalists with leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Redesign how media monitoring, journalist research and coverage reporting work using AI, and set the workflows up so the rest of the team can use them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and improve the team&#39;s media management tool, and check every AI-assisted pitch, briefing or summary before it reaches a journalist.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Fluency Level 3:&lt;/strong&gt; in this role that means you have gone well beyond using AI to draft copy. You have redesigned parts of how media relations work gets done, such as monitoring, journalist research or coverage reporting, you have built approaches that colleagues now follow, and you actively question and check what AI gives you, including target lists, summaries and quotes, before anything reaches a journalist or a spokesperson.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;For more information on AI fluency at Mews, please refer to &lt;a href=&quot;https://mews.atlassian.net/wiki/x/XQOskg&quot;&gt;AI Fluency at Mews: A Comprehensive Guide for Candidates&lt;/a&gt; on Confluence.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you would bring&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Seven to ten years in PR and communications with depth in B2B media relations, including time in a PR agency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your own journalist contacts and hands-on experience pitching by phone, email and in person, with fully fluent English, written and spoken.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A record of handling reactive and sensitive press enquiries under time pressure, with clear habits about when to escalate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidence preparing senior and non-expert spokespeople for press conversations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI Fluency Level 3 or the equivalent hands-on experience, shown through tools or workflows you have built for media relations work, not only content you have written with AI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Nice to have&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;French or German alongside fluent English, or existing relationships with journalists in the UK, France, Germany or the US.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with B2B technology clients or in hospitality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience measuring coverage and coordinating local expertise in markets where you have fewer contacts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;UK&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;£59,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;£77,000 GBP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;France&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$60,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$80,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Ireland&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$70,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$92,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Transparency at Mews&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Salary ranges are provided in good faith and reflect current market conditions and internal pay structures. Final compensation may be adjusted based on funding, budget constraints, or exceptional candidate qualifications, but will remain within reasonable proximity to the stated range.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This salary disclosure is provided in compliance with applicable pay transparency legislation. We are committed to equal pay practices and prohibit salary history inquiries during our recruitment process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If the location you&#39;re applying from wasn&#39;t originally advertised for this role, salary range information is available upon request at any point during the application/interview process - your recruiter will be able to help.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What’s in it for you?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our success is powered by our incredible people, supported by benefits that help them thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;No matter where you’re based, you’ll enjoy:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unlimited paid holiday (yes, really)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participation in our company share program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid parental leave (6 months fully paid for primary caregivers, 2 months for secondary, available after one year of service)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An annual Learning budget of €300 (and more for high performers) to support your development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly &quot;EDGE&quot; time to Explore, Develop, Grow, and Elevate yourself&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A work from anywhere policy with flexibility to work abroad for a few weeks each year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relocation options, available after one year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible, hybrid working options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A home office setup budget to make your workspace your own and a monthly work-from-home allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Claude tokens, so you can automate workflows and build smarter, more efficient ways of working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Local benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll receive additional benefits that vary by location, from healthcare and retirement plans to team events, socials and other perks. Ask us about it during your interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Life at Mews&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re an equal opportunities employer. We value teams that reflect the diversity of the customers and communities we serve. Different perspectives make better ideas, stronger products and a more welcoming company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We also believe transparency is important when deciding if you&#39;re the right fit. Mews is an ambitious, high-pressure environment of continuous learning and high standards. Success here requires resilience, adaptability and a willingness to solve difficult problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A few things that define how we work:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High autonomy means high responsibility. People are expected to take ownership and drive outcomes. There isn’t a detailed playbook for everything, and that’s part of what makes the work challenging – and rewarding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Change is constant. We’re growing quickly and adapting as we scale. Teams, processes and priorities continue to evolve, and only people who stay curious and agile will thrive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We’re remote-first, not relationship-free. Flexibility is core to how we work, but strong relationships still matter. Our teams are global, so we need expert collaborators and communicators to help us move forward together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI is an integral part of our processes. It’s not here to steal people’s jobs, but to amplify efficiency and productivity. We’re motivated to proactively use the technology to seek out better ways of working and share our findings with the rest of the company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If there&#39;s anything we can do to support you during the application process, let us know.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We don&#39;t discriminate on the basis of race, religion, colour, nationality, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, disability or any other protected characteristic.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;One final thing: don&#39;t hold back. If you don&#39;t meet 100% of the criteria in this job description but you&#39;re certain you could make a big impact, apply. Everyone should have equal access to opportunities, and we&#39;re committed to providing an inclusive experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If Mews sounds like the kind of environment where you&#39;d thrive, we&#39;d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;Start: immediately | Level: Intermediate | Location: Switzerland, remote | Working hours: Full-time (40h/week)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;More Nutrition already has a very large presence in Switzerland with an 8-digit revenue, double digit growth and significant investment. Our presence has been anchored into the German-speaking part of Switzerland; we’re set to expand while growing our presence in Romandy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Marketing Manager, you will report into the VP, International, and will be responsible for developing and executing our brand strategy for More Nutrition in Switzerland, with a particular focus on Romandy. You will also start seeding the French market. Speaking French is MANDATORY.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will create impactful campaigns, drive local marketing initiatives and ensure a consistent brand experience across all touchpoints. You will work closely with cross-functional teams, agencies and local stakeholders to significantly expand our presence in the Swiss market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ve got a good understanding of cultural nuances between German-speaking Swizterland, Romandy and France. You’ve worked in a fast-paced consumer goods or FMCG environment, operating both with big retailers and direct online sales platforms. You’re comfortable in newly created roles, working with multiple functional stakeholders, and can roll up your sleeves to execute.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Your mission&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· As brand guardian, you develop and implement the brand strategy for Switzerland, combining global guidelines with local consumer insights&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· You define the marketing activation calendar and lead the planning and execution of omnichannel campaigns (incl. mass media, influencer marketing, TikTok and point of sale)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· You brief and manage agencies to create on-brand, locally relevant assets (in German and French) and ensure timely campaign delivery&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· You track brand metrics (awareness, equity, engagement) and campaign KPIs and use this data for continuous optimisation&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· You work closely with cross-functional teams to guarantee a consistent brand experience across D2C, pure play and point of sale&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· You coordinate closely with the local commercial teams to align marketing activities with market and sales targets&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· You help shape the local product portfolio based on the needs and potential of the Swiss market&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Your experience &amp;amp; skills&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· French speaking is mandatory Ideally you have experience working both in French-speaking Swizterland and France. You have some level of understanding of how the shopper may differ.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· You have 4–6 years of solid professional experience as a brand or marketing manager in FMCG / consumer goods, ideally in food &amp;amp; beverage&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· You have proven experience leading or managing one or more brands in Switzerland or France with revenues of at least CHF 30 million&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· You have solid experience managing a D2C business and omnichannel campaigns (incl. mass media, influencer marketing, social media such as TikTok and Meta, as well as point of sale + pure play)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· You stand out with a strong hands-on mentality, excellent project management skills and a genuine enthusiasm for cross-functional collaboration&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· You have a data-driven mindset and are confident using digital marketing tools&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· You are fluent in French and are confident using English for our internal communication. Speaking German is of course a definite plus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Why us?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At The Quality Group, more than 1,200 people share a common mission: to rethink nutrition – healthier, smarter and with real added value for the community. We believe in team spirit, ownership and the courage to push boundaries. Every contribution counts, regardless of location or department. Depending on where you join us, you can look forward to various benefits, including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Attractive employee discounts on ESN &amp;amp; More products&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Flexible working hours &amp;amp; home office options&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Workation options and more&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;During the application process, you&#39;ll find out which specific benefits await you at your location and what it means to be part of TQG: a company shaping the future of nutrition with passion, quality and courage.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Quality Group (TQG) is an innovative provider of sports nutrition products and has united the successful brands ESN and More Nutrition since 2021. ESN has been Germany&#39;s market leader in sports nutrition since 2004, offering products such as protein powders, bars and supplements designed for ambitious fitness goals. More Nutrition, founded in 2017, stands for healthy, sugar-reduced nutrition products and offers solutions for mindful eating and weight management – without sacrifice. TQG&#39;s vision is to help people become the best version of themselves. With passion and innovative strength, the company develops high-quality products that promote health, performance and joy of life. With an agile corporate culture and exciting career opportunities, TQG is a strong partner not only for customers but also for employees. That&#39;s us – The Quality Group – nice to meet you! Now it&#39;s your turn! We look forward to receiving your application! Regardless of gender, age, background or identity – what matters to us is who you are and what you bring. Join our team and grow with us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;Suisse de préférence, France à discuter, télétravail&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Début : dès que possible | Niveau : Intermédiaire | Lieu : Suisse, télétravail | Temps de travail : temps plein (40 h/semaine)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;More Nutrition bénéficie déjà d’une très forte présence en Suisse, avec un chiffre d’affaires à 8 chiffres, une croissance à deux chiffres et des investissements importants. Notre présence s’est jusqu’ici ancrée en Suisse alémanique ; nous souhaitons à présent poursuivre notre expansion en renforçant notre présence en Romandie.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;En tant que Marketing Manager, tu seras rattaché(e) au VP International et seras responsable du développement et de la mise en œuvre de notre stratégie de marque pour More Nutrition en Suisse, avec un focus particulier sur la Romandie. Tu commenceras également à nous positionner sur le marché français.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dans ce rôle, tu exécuteras nos campagnes de marque, piloteras les initiatives marketing locales et garantiras une expérience de marque cohérente. Tu travailleras en étroite collaboration avec les équipes commerciales, DTC, marketing, produits…, les agences et autres partenaires locaux.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tu as une bonne compréhension des nuances culturelles entre la Suisse alémanique, la Romandie et la France. Tu as de l’expérience en biens de consommation ou FMCG dans des environnements dynamiques et as travaillé à la fois avec de grandes enseignes et des plateformes D2C. Tu es à l’aise dans des postes nouvellement créés, tu sais collaborer avec différentes fonctions et tu es orienté(e) action.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Merci de nous envoyer ton dossier de candidature en anglais.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ta mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;· En tant que gardien(ne) de la marque, tu développes et mets en œuvre la stratégie de marque pour la Suisse, en associant guidelines globales et insights consommateurs locaux&lt;br&gt;· Tu définis le calendrier d’activation et pilotes la planification et l’exécution de campagnes omnicanales (médias de masse, marketing d’influence, TikTok et point de vente inclus)&lt;br&gt;· Tu briefes et pilotes les agences pour créer des contenus conformes à la marque et adaptés localement (en allemand et en français)&lt;br&gt;· Tu suis les indicateurs de marque (notoriété, capital de marque, engagement) ainsi que les KPI de campagne et tu les optimises continuellement&lt;br&gt;· Tu travailles en étroite collaboration avec des équipes transverses pour garantir une expérience de marque cohérente sur tous les canaux&lt;br&gt;· Tu adaptes l’assortiment local en fonction des besoins et du potentiel du marché suisse (et français)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ton expérience &amp;amp; tes compétences&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;·&amp;nbsp;La maîtrise du français est obligatoire. Idéalement, tu as de l’expérience à la fois en Suisse romande et en France. Tu comprends les différences de comportement entre consommateurs suisses et français.&lt;br&gt;· Tu as 4 à 6 ans d’expérience professionnelle en tant que Brand Manager ou Marketing Manager en FMCG / biens de consommation, idéalement en Food &amp;amp; Beverage.&lt;br&gt;· Tu as géré une ou plusieurs marques en Suisse ou en France générant un chiffre d’affaires d’au moins 30 millions CHF.&lt;br&gt;· Tu as une solide expérience dans la gestion d’un business D2C et de campagnes omnicanales (médias de masse, marketing d’influence, réseaux sociaux comme TikTok et Meta, ainsi que point de vente + pure players).&lt;br&gt;· Tu te distingues par un fort esprit opérationnel, d’excellentes compétences en gestion de projet et un fort esprit de collaboration.&lt;br&gt;· Tu es analytique et maîtrises les outils de marketing digital.&lt;br&gt;· Tu parles couramment français et utilises l’anglais avec aisance au quotidien dans un contexte professionnel. Parler allemand est un atout.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Pourquoi nous ?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Chez The Quality Group, plus de 1 200 personnes partagent une mission commune : repenser la nutrition – plus saine, plus intelligente et avec une réelle valeur ajoutée pour la communauté. Nous croyons en l’esprit d’équipe, à la responsabilité individuelle et au courage de repousser les limites. Chaque contribution compte, quel que soit le site ou le service. Selon l’endroit où tu nous rejoins, différents avantages t’attendent, notamment :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Des réductions attractives pour les collaborateurs sur les produits ESN &amp;amp; More&lt;br&gt;· Des horaires flexibles &amp;amp; des possibilités de télétravail&lt;br&gt;· Des options de workation et plus encore&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Au cours du processus de recrutement, tu découvriras les avantages concrets proposés sur ton site et ce que signifie faire partie de TQG : une entreprise qui façonne l’avenir de la nutrition avec passion, qualité et courage.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;À propos de nous&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Quality Group (TQG) est un fournisseur innovant de produits de nutrition sportive qui réunit depuis 2021 les marques à succès ESN et More Nutrition. ESN est depuis 2004 le leader du marché allemand de la nutrition sportive et propose des produits tels que des protéines en poudre, des barres et des compléments alimentaires adaptés aux objectifs de fitness ambitieux. More Nutrition, fondée en 2017, est synonyme de produits nutritionnels sains et à teneur réduite en sucre, et propose des solutions pour une alimentation consciente et la gestion du poids – sans privation. La vision de TQG est d’aider chacun à devenir la meilleure version de lui-même. Avec passion et esprit d’innovation, l’entreprise développe des produits de haute qualité qui favorisent la santé, la performance et la joie de vivre. Grâce à une culture d’entreprise agile et à des opportunités de carrière passionnantes, TQG est un partenaire solide non seulement pour ses clients, mais aussi pour ses collaborateurs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;C’est nous – The Quality Group – ravis de te rencontrer ! À toi de jouer ! Nous nous réjouissons de recevoir ta candidature ! Quel que soit ton genre, ton âge, ton origine ou ton identité – ce qui compte pour nous, c’est qui tu es et ce que tu apportes. Rejoins notre équipe et grandis avec nous.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h2&gt;Who is Artefact?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Artefact is a next-generation strategy and data consulting firm dedicated to transforming organisations through data and AI. We combine the rigour of top-tier strategy consulting with deep expertise in data, digital and analytics to help clients achieve tangible business impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With 2,500+ consultants, data scientists and engineers, we work with global leaders such as Samsung, L’Oréal, Orange and Sanofi. Our Swiss offices are at the heart of Artefact’s growth, advising clients on their most pressing strategic challenges — from AI strategy and governance to digital transformation roadmaps and new business model design.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Main Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Consultant in our Zurich/Lausanne office, you will work at the intersection of strategy consulting and data and AI delivery. You will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategy Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Work with client leadership teams to address high-stakes questions. How can AI reshape our business model? How should we govern and organise for data? Which strategic programmes deliver the most impact?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Structured Problem-Solving:&lt;/strong&gt; Break complex challenges down into decisions a client can act on, combining consulting rigour with a working knowledge of what current AI can and cannot actually do.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Solution Design:&lt;/strong&gt; Turn a business question into a solution shape — what data it depends on, what kind of platform or product it should sit on, and what “good” looks like once it is built. You will do this alongside our data scientists and engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Project Delivery:&lt;/strong&gt; Support engagements end to end, from hypothesis framing and market and competitor analysis through to data maturity assessments, client workshops, governance design and implementation roadmaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client Engagement:&lt;/strong&gt; Work closely with C-level stakeholders and business unit leaders. You will build trusted relationships, communicate recommendations with clarity, and keep the work aligned to what the client is actually trying to decide.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Knowledge &amp;amp; Practice Building:&lt;/strong&gt; Contribute to the growth of Artefact&#39;s Zurich office by shaping new offerings, creating intellectual capital - frameworks, thought pieces, benchmarks - and taking part in business development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Candidate Profile&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for someone who can hold a technical position and a commercial one at the same time. The strongest candidates meet most of the following.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education:&lt;/strong&gt; A degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Data Science, Business, Economics or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; Around three to five years in consulting, or in a technical/date-focussed role with client-facing responsibility.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business Acumen &amp;amp; AI Fluency:&lt;/strong&gt; A genuine dual affinity for business and technology. You are comfortable with modern data and AI concepts - generative AI and LLMs, retrieval, predictive machine learning, cloud platforms - and with what they cost and where they fail, not only with what they are called.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Depth:&lt;/strong&gt; You have built AI or data products, not only advised on them. You can explain why you chose which model you put on which part of the work, and what that choice did to both output quality and cost. You will not be writing production code in this role, but you should have the basic understanding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical &amp;amp; Problem-Solving Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong quantitative and analytical skills, and the judgement to know which number actually decides the question. You are comfortable getting to a defensible estimate with your assumptions stated out loud.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication &amp;amp; Interpersonal Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; Excellent written and verbal communication. You enjoy working in teams and in front of clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Languages:&lt;/strong&gt; Fluency in German/French and English, written and spoken, is strongly preferred..&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Eligibility:&lt;/strong&gt; You must be eligible to work in Switzerland.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why Join Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategy and the Build:&lt;/strong&gt; Artefact is neither a traditional strategy consultancy nor a pure technology player. You will move between the boardroom and the build, and be expected to be credible in both.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engineers, not hand-offs:&lt;/strong&gt; Our 2,500 people include the data scientists and engineers you will work beside on the same engagement - not a delivery organisation you hand a slide deck to.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Zurich Office Impact:&lt;/strong&gt; As part of a growing Swiss team you will have visibility and impact from the first day. You will help shape Artefact&#39;s footprint in the region and work directly with senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learning &amp;amp; Growth:&lt;/strong&gt; Regular training in both consulting method and AI and data capability, combined with international exposure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Culture of Doers:&lt;/strong&gt; Innovation, action, collaboration. We are entrepreneurial and fast-moving, committed to delivering impact while supporting each other&#39;s growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is based in &lt;strong&gt;Zürich or Lausanne&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

